      "content": "The most equitable approach is a needs-based, tiered system prioritizing income level. This ensures that the units directly benefit those who need them most, which is the core purpose of affordable housing. A lottery system is inherently unfair because it ignores economic reality, while transit proximity alone doesn't address financial hardship.",
