      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The principle of equal opportunity is meaningless when people lack the basic resources to participate in society. Social engineering, in this context, is simply the necessary mechanism to correct the deep structural inequalities that prevent true opportunity for the poor. A system that guarantees shelter to those who are most vulnerable is not \"social engineering\"; it is fulfilling a fundamental moral obligation of a functioning society.",
      "source": "target",
